# SysWatch runtime data.
#
# Ignored by directory, not by filename. The individual patterns below cover
# syswatch.db and syswatch.log, but not a rotated syswatch.log.3, a
# VACUUM INTO backup, or anything else the application writes next to them —
# and everything in here is either the monitored machine's own telemetry or a
# session secret.
backend/data/
agent/logs/

# Any SQLite database, wherever it lands — not just the one named syswatch.db.
# `app.db.backup` takes an arbitrary destination path, so a backup written from
# the repository root is a plausible accident, and the file it produces carries
# every account's argon2 password hash and every live session token hash. WAL
# mode writes the -wal and -shm sidecars alongside it.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Key material. None of this exists in the project today; these are here so that
# the first time it does, it is already ignored rather than ignored afterwards.
*.pem
*.key
*.pfx
*.p12
*.jks
*.keystore
id_rsa
id_rsa.*
id_ecdsa
id_ed25519

# Deployment inputs that hold values rather than describing them.
secrets.json
secrets.yml
secrets.yaml
deploy/*.local.*

# Dashboard (Node / Vite). node_modules is thousands of files restored from
# package-lock.json, so it never belongs in the repository. The build output
# lands in dashboard/dist, already covered by the dist/ rule further up.
node_modules/
.vite/
dashboard/dist-ssr/
*.local
npm-debug.log*
